1
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:11,120
Lighten up and try stepping back, would you?

2
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone without money, come to my place.

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,980
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

4
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,800
Look at the blue sky.

5
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,160
White clouds.

6
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:56,000
Ohara, what's the exact time right now?

7
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,340
Yes, it's currently 9:59:48.

8
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:03,220
That's twelve seconds
before the appointment.

9
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:10,540
I hear they're extremely strict about time.
That's why they've been summoning us one after another.

10
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:15,060
We can't afford any blunders, Ohara.
Let's go!

11
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:21,200
Ohara of the Katsushika police box, reporting.
Come in. Excuse us.

12
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:28,160
Sorry to have made you
two come all this way.

13
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:29,840
N-not at all!

14
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,840
U-um, our idiot...

15
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:32,194
No, well...

16
00:02:32,244 --> 00:02:35,880
Has Ryotsu done something outrageous again?

17
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:36,700
Ryotsu?

18
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:39,820
The famous man of Katsushika Station's

19
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:43,740
No, I asked you to come today
because I have a favor to ask of you.

20
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:45,940
A favor?

21
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:48,940
Before that,
let me introduce this gentleman.

22
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:49,960
Mr. Tsukuda.

23
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:52,820
Tomita-kun, long time no see.

24
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,680
I-it's been a long time, sir.

25
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:01,780
Ohara, why are you spacing out?

26
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:04,720
This gentleman is Honorary
Superintendent Tsukuda.

27
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:06,240
Honorary Superintendent?

28
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:11,620
The one they call the
gatekeeper of Sakuradamon,

29
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:14,060
Excuse me.

30
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:18,060
Bowing like that makes it
harder to ask you a favor.

31
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:19,420
Please, look up.

32
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:23,280
Actually, Mr. Tsukuda retires tomorrow.

33
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:26,940
Yes, that's right. Even though he was an elite career officer,
he devoted himself solely to the field,

34
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:31,800
and it was Honorary Superintendent Tsukuda
who personally led and solved the cases.

35
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:37,440
He really should have become Commissioner-General before me,
you know.

36
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:41,240
No, no.
I'm not the type to stand at the top.

37
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:45,160
So what is Honorary
Superintendent Tsukuda's request?

38
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:50,220
Before he retires, he wants to work at
the police box for just one day tomorrow.

39
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:52,080
The honorary superintendent wants that?

40
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:57,040
Ever since he joined the police, he always
wanted to serve at a police box just once.

41
00:03:58,220 --> 00:04:02,140
Please, could you make Mr.
Tsukuda's lifelong dream come true?

42
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:16,020
Understood. We will take full responsibility and make the honorary superintendent's day a memorable one. Thank you.
Also, since it would be troublesome for the police box staff, please keep it quiet that I'm an honorary superintendent.

43
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:21,480
Keep that secret, all right? Certainly.
Then tomorrow morning at nine.

44
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:23,860
You two, I'm counting on you. Haa.

45
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:30,220
A wonderful day for
Super Senior Citizen-san.

46
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:37,600
He's late.

47
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:40,520
It's already seven minutes past nine!

48
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,420
Maybe the roads are congested, do you think?

49
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,580
Ohara-kun.

50
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:50,000
What if he went straight
to the Hashisuji station?

51
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,580
W-what did you say?

52
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,640
This is bad, Ohara-kun.

53
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:59,580
If he goes there directly and
sees that man's work situation,

54
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:03,140
our heads will definitely fly off!

55
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,460
This is a serious emergency, Chief.

56
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:06,600
Hurry, Ohara-kun!

57
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:11,440
So you're retiring today?

58
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:14,400
I'll only be working for one day,
but please take care of me.

59
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:17,100
The pleasure is all ours,
please take care of us.

60
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:18,800
Move, move, move, move, move!

61
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:31,660
Ouch

62
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:31,700
Ouch

63
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:32,000
Ouch

64
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:32,200
Ouch

65
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:32,300
Ouch

66
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:32,620
Ouch

67
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:33,040
Ouch

68
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:33,100
Ouch

69
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:33,120
Ouch

70
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:33,140
Ouch

71
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:33,180
Ouch

72
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:33,220
Ouch

73
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:33,360
Ouch

74
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:33,500
Ouch

75
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:33,540
Ouch

76
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:42,860
Ouch

77
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:49,760
Ouch!

78
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:52,600
What's this old geezer?

79
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:56,600
Tsukuda, who's going to be working
at this station just for today.

80
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,640
I'm a patrolman.

81
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:00,200
A patrolman? At your age, still a patrolman?

82
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:06,460
Tsukuda or tsukudani, whatever you are,
you must be one useless cop.

83
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:08,920
Senpai, that's rude.

84
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,340
Yes, Ryo-chan, apologize right now.

85
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:15,700
That's why they keep employing
useless old men like this.

86
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:18,340
And that's why my salary never goes up.

87
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:23,300
You can say that, when you're
always causing trouble for everyone.

88
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:23,880
Shut up.

89
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:25,440
Tsukudani.

90
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,640
I'm Tsukuda.

91
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:31,460
Names don't matter. Pass me that red pencil.

92
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:34,980
Senpai, Mr. Tsukuda is a patrolman,
but he's your senior.

93
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:37,320
Senior or not, a patrolman is a patrolman.

94
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:39,460
I'm a senior patrolman, and I outrank you.

95
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:43,320
It's rare for someone your
age to be a senior patrolman.

96
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:46,900
You, a perpetual patrolman, saying that?

97
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,128
Aaah!

98
00:06:48,178 --> 00:06:51,160
What do you think you're
doing to Mr. Tsukuda!

99
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:55,300
Chief Ohara,
what are you doing all of a sudden!

100
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:58,560
Yo-tsu! Do you know who this gentleman is!

101
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:02,540
What are you talking about,
like Mito Kōmon? Chief?

102
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:04,216
This gentleman is, you see...

103
00:07:04,266 --> 00:07:07,720
We promised not to reveal his true identity.

104
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:10,140
What's wrong, Chief?

105
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:11,800
N-nothing.

106
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,500
But we were in the middle of talking...

107
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:17,900
Don't get cocky just because
that gentleman is Officer Tsukuda.

108
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:19,380
Understood.

109
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:21,520
He's quite interesting.

110
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:23,560
Well then, for the whole day today,

111
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:27,260
I'll be acting as Senior
Patrolman Ryotsu's assistant.

112
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:30,960
Isn't that a bit of a reckless idea?

113
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:31,540
Interesting.

114
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:34,760
Let's go on patrol with Tsukuda,
the eternal patrolman.

115
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:37,760
Ryotsu, watch your language, okay?

116
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,380
Well then, I'm off.

117
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:44,620
Chief Ohara,
we're definitely getting the axe!

118
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,880
Chief, what on earth is the matter?

119
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:51,700
Are you disrespecting his honorary status?

120
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,360
So he was that important a person?

121
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:58,220
Lamenting won't help, Ohara.

122
00:07:58,220 --> 00:07:59,220
Yes, indeed.

123
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:03,100
Let's keep an eye on Ryotsu so he
doesn't do anything rude to Mr. Tsukuda.

124
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:05,340
He spent a long time in the
First Investigation Division.

125
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:07,440
Just a lifelong patrolman, and yet...

126
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:11,320
So which station are you from?

127
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:12,800
Headquarters, of course.

128
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,360
Don't lie to me.

129
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,200
I warned that idiot so many times!

130
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:21,100
That's terrible for my heart.

131
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:23,240
Enough with the jokes.

132
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:27,120
We're not the Investigation Unit,
we're the Cleaning Unit.

133
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:30,380
Nice one, Yamada! A cushion for you!

134
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:32,640
You're pretty fun for your age, aren't you?

135
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:35,660
You're way younger than our
station chief and Chief Ohara.

136
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:36,640
Well, thanks.

137
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,740
Lucky! It's a fresh machine,
spinning like crazy!

138
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:48,840
When they open,
they hand out balls like crazy as a service.

139
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,140
Let's go.

140
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,960
Is that guy always like that?

141
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:56,120
Well, with those balls...

142
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:58,100
Welcome, welcome!

143
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:00,060
At the Osaka Pachinko entertainment hall...

144
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:02,760
Woo-hoo, jackpot!

145
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:06,080
Whoa, heavy, heavy!

146
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:13,600
Ryo-san, isn't playing pachinko on patrol a bad idea?
This is part of the patrol.

147
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:18,100
Hey, you're not bad yourself. Have a go!

148
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:31,860
You look like a lousy player,
but I'll let you have a little of that.

149
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:35,940
Hey, Ryotsu, stop it! I'm sick of this.

150
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:39,340
What's wrong with that?
This machine is mine.

151
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:46,520
I left my cigarettes and went to the bathroom.
See? That's why I stopped by here.

152
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:53,580
You've been playing nonstop. Liar, I sat
down here the moment it stopped spinning.

153
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:56,880
I just put this down right now, didn't I?

154
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:58,320
How old-fashioned.

155
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:02,100
Making excuses like that is
so old-fashioned these days.

156
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:03,860
That stinks!

157
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:07,780
You barked so loud!

158
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:10,260
I'll let it slide, alright?

159
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:16,660
Old man! It's terrible!

160
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:18,280
Come quick!

161
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:20,200
What's wrong, old man Tsukuda?

162
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,600
Old man?

163
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:23,360
It's a jackpot!

164
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:26,180
Let me have a go! I'll take it from here.

165
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:30,040
Yay, jackpot!

166
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:31,960
Beginner's luck

167
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:39,820
I'd never tried it before,
but I didn't expect it to be this much fun.

168
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:43,480
That's exactly why you've
been a patrolman forever.

169
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:47,460
Do you really think you can be a police officer
if you don't understand how ordinary people feel?

170
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:49,040
I see.

171
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:53,120
Ryotsu's lecturing us.
The nerve of him, isn't it?

172
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:57,780
By the way, what's your family like?

173
00:10:57,780 --> 00:10:59,220
What's with the sudden question?

174
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:04,220
No reason, I just figured a dad like
you must be strict with his daughter.

175
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:10,060
The honorary official has finally snapped!

176
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:13,120
What's wrong, Tsukuda, old man?

177
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:17,000
Nothing, I just slipped a little.

178
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,980
Well, let's get back to patrol.

179
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:23,100
You might want to write
it all up for the record.

180
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,360
Let's stop by for a sec.

181
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:31,720
This photo book series comes out today.

182
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,800
Pichi Pichi Onee-san

183
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:36,600
Muhi Tamago

184
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:41,580
Isn't it a bad idea to buy them in uniform?

185
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:45,260
That idiot...

186
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:49,340
Now, where's the photo book section?

187
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,920
Hold it, high schooler.

188
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:03,880
If you take one step out of this bookstore with that,
it's a crime!

189
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:06,040
I'm sorry.

190
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:09,920
Hey, Tsukuda old man,
take this back to the shelf for me.

191
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,600
Alright, let's go.

192
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:27,060
Well, go ahead with the mental arithmetic.

193
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:30,980
Aren't we taking him to the police box?

194
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:35,740
He seems to be a first-time offender, and
he's remorseful, so there's no need for that.

195
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,920
Then where?

196
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:39,240
My room at the Nikoniko Dormitory.

197
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:43,240
Haul all this out, start cleaning!

198
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:45,700
Dust it all off.

199
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:47,180
Here, the vacuum cleaner.

200
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:48,160
Good.

201
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:50,380
Yes, and wring out the rags properly too.

202
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:52,920
Come on, come on, more fighting spirit!

203
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:53,840
Put your back into it!

204
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:55,960
Good, keep it up.

205
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,540
Alright, that's about enough.

206
00:12:58,540 --> 00:12:59,500
Well done.

207
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,400
Can I go home now?

208
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:03,040
Hold on a second.

209
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:05,120
This one.

210
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,280
Whoa, what a treasure!

211
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:11,800
I'll give you all of that,

212
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,040
so don't go selling it off, got it?

213
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:17,000
Come on, hurry up and pack it all into this.

214
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:18,620
You can go home now.

215
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:20,580
Make sure you don't go to the bathhouse.

216
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,860
Right, then, I'll be taking my leave.

217
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:26,440
That was a masterful Ōoka-style judgment,
wasn't it?

218
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:28,100
I've changed my opinion of you.

219
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:31,060
Cleaning the room and getting rid of
the photo books you didn't need anymore,

220
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,460
that's all I did, really.

221
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,340
Incident!

222
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:36,920
Let's go, old man!

223
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:58,420
Tough luck

224
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,980
You're the unlucky one here.

225
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:03,920
Take this!

226
00:14:10,340 --> 00:14:12,420
Tsukuda, old man, cuff him!

227
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:16,700
Because you've never
once arrested a criminal.

228
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:18,180
You're a perpetual patrolman, aren't you?

229
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:20,260
I'll let you take the credit, old man.

230
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:21,560
Shoot already!

231
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:24,220
Well then, if you insist,
I'll take you up on that.

232
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:26,180
Take this!

233
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:27,420
Nice!

234
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:29,680
So close!

235
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:32,460
Go, go, Pops!

236
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:34,200
Move! You'll get hurt!

237
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:35,420
Nyaa!

238
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:37,120
Toh!

239
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:39,700
Ugh, nah!

240
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:42,020
Urgh!

241
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,780
Gah, agh...

242
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:53,500
Mr. Tsukuda,
you're really something, aren't you?

243
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:58,100
Well, I've practiced judo for years,
so it's the one thing I've got down.

244
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:08,020
Old man, great work. Leave the rest to me.

245
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,280
Yes, once I've rested,
I'll head straight back to the box.

246
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:12,740
Right, I'll be waiting.

247
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:21,060
I'm a bit hungry. I'll stuff myself
with some ramen before heading back.

248
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:23,680
What's this, a letter?

249
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:27,300
Did the old man Tsukuda drop it?

250
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:29,540
Sure enough.

251
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:31,640
So he has a daughter.

252
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:36,100
Let's see...
"Dear Father and Mother, how are you doing?"

253
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:40,520
"It's been five years since I ran out of the house,
defying your objections."

254
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:44,720
Forgive me for sending
this postcard so late.

255
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:48,360
Back then, Akira, as my father said,

256
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,660
had gone astray and grown
reckless and desperate.

257
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:53,560
But now he has completely reformed.

258
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:57,020
Last month,
he opened a ramen shop in Katsushika.

259
00:15:57,020 --> 00:16:00,500
The ramen that his father
and mother made together

260
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,360
Please come and try it sometime.

261
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:04,860
At this address,
it's in front of the station?

262
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:05,700
Ryo-chan.

263
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:07,760
What's going on with you two?

264
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:09,800
Dressed up like Inspector Zenigata?

265
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,840
That doesn't matter.

266
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:13,740
Where's the honorary officer?

267
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,040
Who is that?

268
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,160
That's Mr. Tsukuda!

269
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:21,100
He's the second most important person
after the Police Commissioner General!

270
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:24,000
That old guy was that important?

271
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:27,740
But why would someone that
important be working at a police box?

272
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:30,520
Hey! I don't have time to explain it to you!

273
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:31,960
Where did you hide him?

274
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:35,200
We arrested the robber
and had him taken away.

275
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,860
That important old guy did it.

276
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,380
He's not an old guy!

277
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,200
Call him Honorary Police Officer Tsukuda!

278
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:43,740
I see, so he's back at the box.

279
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:47,440
Anyway, Chief, Director,
please look at this.

280
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:49,060
What is that?

281
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:58,360
I never expected the honorary police
inspector's daughter to have eloped.

282
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:01,040
So that solves the mystery, Chief.

283
00:17:01,040 --> 00:17:02,240
Yes, it's solved.

284
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:02,980
Mystery.

285
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:06,820
There are so many police
boxes all over Tokyo,

286
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:11,260
so I wondered why she chose
the Kameari Park-mae police box.

287
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:15,200
She probably wanted to
check on the young lady.

288
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:18,460
I wish we could somehow reunite them.

289
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:23,980
If that's the case, she could just tell me,
but she's not very honest, is she, Nyarun.

290
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:28,160
Bakaron, do you think someone like you could
understand how a parent with a daughter feels?

291
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:32,320
Ohara, let's just go check
out that ramen shop for now.

292
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:35,280
Right. Going by the address on the postcard,

293
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:37,820
well, in that case, I'll show you the way.

294
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:41,260
It's over there.

295
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:43,400
It's quite popular, isn't it.

296
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:46,020
So it's a specialty shop
for Tokyo-style ramen.

297
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:48,780
If it comes to this,
I'll go out on a limb for you.

298
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:51,040
I wonder if there's a difference
between light and dark?

299
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:51,860
There is.

300
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:53,900
Leave it to me.

301
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:57,660
Thanks for walking us over.

302
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:01,800
Chief Ohara

303
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:04,060
You don't even know the
first thing about flavor.

304
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:06,080
Don't go acting like an expert.

305
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,120
Shut up!

306
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:13,780
What did you say, Ohara? The loudest one here is you!
What's gotten into you three?

307
00:18:13,780 --> 00:18:23,520
Tsukuda! Old man, you're back at the right time.
Listen, we're about to go eat ramen, and I'm a fan of the light, Tokyo-style kind.

308
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:33,460
I'm asking about ramen, and these two say miso Sapporo ramen!
No, rich tonkotsu Hakata ramen!

309
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,700
So that's what you were arguing about?

310
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:41,060
Old man, which ramen do you like?

311
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:44,580
Being a true Edokko,
I'll go with Tokyo ramen.

312
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:47,520
Right? Alright, Tokyo ramen it is!

313
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:52,260
I know a great place,
so I'll treat all four of us.

314
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:54,840
Nice, Ryo-san's treating us.

315
00:18:56,660 --> 00:19:00,480
Rossi, four guests, please take the counter.

316
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:01,600
Coming right up!

317
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:03,160
Thanks for the meal. Just leave it here.

318
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:04,940
Thank you very much for your patronage.

319
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,060
Only two items on the menu

320
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:10,360
They must be really
confident in their taste.

321
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:12,600
Four ramen and a beer.

322
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:14,440
No beer.

323
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:16,140
Four ramen.

324
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:20,960
Impressive work.

325
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:22,880
You must have trained
for at least ten years.

326
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:24,040
No, no.

327
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:25,560
I'm still just a novice with
five years under my belt.

328
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:27,600
Here you are, thanks for waiting.

329
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,560
Sorry to keep you waiting.

330
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:30,340
This is delicious.

331
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:32,480
This broth is great, old man.

332
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:36,700
Yeah, the noodles soak up the soup so well,
it's delicious.

333
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:37,520
Thank you very much.

334
00:19:38,540 --> 00:19:42,100
The place is nice,
and your parents must be so proud.

335
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:43,600
Of course they are.

336
00:19:44,460 --> 00:19:45,280
Yeah, well.

337
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:46,620
I'm home.

338
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:57,860
Are you hurt, Minori?

339
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,720
F-Father?

340
00:20:08,060 --> 00:20:09,480
Thank you for coming to see me.

341
00:20:09,940 --> 00:20:11,320
No, that's not it.

342
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:13,700
These guys said they wanted ramen, so

343
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:14,960
I just tagged along.

344
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:18,380
Don't give me that tough talk,
old man Tsukuda.

345
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:20,800
No matter how moved you are.

346
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:24,060
Where's the parent who doesn't
want to see their only daughter?

347
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:25,520
So that's how it was.

348
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:28,760
Ryotsu's fight was just a ruse

349
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:30,520
to get me here, a sham performance.

350
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:32,620
So that means that

351
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:37,160
I didn't get my hopes up, but I was
completely taken in by Ryotsu's sweet talk.

352
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:39,520
I found this.

353
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:42,940
It fell out when you threw that robber,
old man.

354
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:45,940
I felt bad about it, but I went and read it.

355
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:47,720
Wait, Father.

356
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,580
Listen to what Minori has to say.

357
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:52,760
Akira was definitely a delinquent.

358
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:56,740
But since then, he's worked so hard
for five years that he barely slept.

359
00:20:56,740 --> 00:20:58,800
At last, at last.

360
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:03,980
We finally created a ramen good
enough to make you accept us both.

361
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:07,040
So I gathered my courage
and wrote the postcard,

362
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:10,800
to let you and Mom see who we are now,

363
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:12,660
and to have you eat our ramen,

364
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:15,000
hoping you would forgive us both.

365
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:15,540
Minori.

366
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:17,360
Dad.

367
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,240
Minori hasn't spent a single day

368
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:22,200
without talking about you and Mom.

369
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,320
Once again,

370
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:24,940
please accept the two of us.

371
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:26,760
You!

372
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:29,100
You dare to run off with
someone else's daughter?

373
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:33,200
Do you have any idea
how worried my wife was?

374
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,580
S-sorry.

375
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,660
Dad, I'm sorry.

376
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:42,720
And from now on, don't call my
daughter by her first name again.

377
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,360
Yes, understood.

378
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:46,460
My daughter.

379
00:21:46,460 --> 00:21:48,220
Then, what about the emotional part?

380
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:51,320
So, he said, accept the two of them.

381
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:53,940
Thank you, Dad.

382
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:57,760
Ryotsu, we're heading home.

383
00:21:57,760 --> 00:21:59,520
Yeah, yeah.
Chief, you're picking up the tab.

384
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:02,460
Drop by often,
and give us some extra service at night.

385
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:03,960
Thank you very much.

386
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:07,060
That was delicious. See you.

387
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:10,460
He's a strict man.

388
00:22:10,460 --> 00:22:13,440
But I understand your
father's feelings, Minori.

389
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:15,380
san.

390
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:17,320
Stop it, Akira.

391
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:19,640
Just call me Minori, like you always have.

392
00:22:20,300 --> 00:22:22,880
But be careful in front of Father for now.

393
00:22:23,660 --> 00:22:25,800
Right, I guess we'll just
have to switch between the two.

394
00:22:27,020 --> 00:22:29,900
Hey, your dad left this behind.

395
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:31,940
When did he...

396
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,740
It's a bankbook.

397
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:39,760
It's what your mother and I saved little
by little from the day you were born.

398
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:41,760
Use it wisely.

399
00:22:42,380 --> 00:22:44,020
Next time, come and eat here together.

400
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:49,900
To think they'd go this far for me...

401
00:22:51,420 --> 00:22:54,000
Thank you, Dad and Mom.

402
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:01,480
Thanks to everyone,
it's been a wonderful day.

403
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:02,860
Thank you so much.

404
00:23:04,740 --> 00:23:05,820
Getting to meet the young lady,

405
00:23:07,140 --> 00:23:10,040
shall we go, Honorary Officer Tsukuda?

406
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:16,580
Ohara, you're lucky to have a
wonderful subordinate like Ryotsu.

407
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:22,220
Well, if I may return your words, the
honorary officer position only lasts one day.

408
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:25,320
I think you're misunderstanding
that man's true nature.

409
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:30,440
Why, why? My subordinate is being praised, so
you should honestly be happy, or I'll kill you!

410
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,840
Take care.

411
00:23:39,700 --> 00:23:44,320
Tsukuda, you'll be free from tomorrow,
so let's play pachinko again.

412
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:46,200
I'll keep you company anytime.

413
00:23:46,820 --> 00:23:51,120
If you like, I'll teach you anything: horse racing,
mahjong, boat racing, bicycle racing.

414
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:55,680
Idiot! How dare you say such
a thing to an honorary officer!

415
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:58,180
Stop it, Chief.

416
00:23:58,180 --> 00:24:02,160
I'm Chief Ohara's wonderful subordinate,
after all.

417
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:20,300
Like someone calling out to me,
after the rain stopped,

418
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:27,140
I walked while looking back,
Gaaja holding my hand,

419
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:34,300
that strange feeling I had back then.

420
00:24:35,500 --> 00:24:39,560
So on the arcade's tiles,

421
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:45,320
I tried walking only on the black ones.

422
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:53,480
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

423
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:57,640
Politicians with their self-important faces,

424
00:24:57,640 --> 00:25:00,960
and the aunties with blue
eyeshadow above their eyes,

425
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:06,540
go on, turn that corner over there.

426
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:11,760
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

427
00:25:12,280 --> 00:25:19,860
Over there is Kameari,
well, surely it's Kameari.

428
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:24,920
Everybody come on over to our town

429
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:26,480
Thank you

430
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:34,780
Whoa, what happened?
My eyebrows and my hair are all gone!

431
00:25:34,780 --> 00:25:37,480
Guess I'll just draw them
on with a marker, then

432
00:25:38,060 --> 00:25:40,800
What kind of eyebrows
did I even have before?

433
00:25:41,560 --> 00:25:43,080
Uh-oh, uh-oh, uh-oh

434
00:25:44,060 --> 00:25:47,440
Next time, Tsurupikario-san, that's not good

435
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:50,920
Over there is Kameariii

436
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:55,140
Mark-it Kameariii

437
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:59,300
Everybody come on over to our town

438
00:26:00,340 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you

